Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: upstream, https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/commit/87b32e3d8102c2da79d711afd8e7bf200fbb201a
From 87b32e3d8102c2da79d711afd8e7bf200fbb201a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:55:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] avformat/mpegts: read ISO/IEC 23002-3 auxiliary video
 streams

An auxiliary video stream (ISO/IEC 13818-1 2.16), a depth or parallax
map for a primary video stream, has stream type 0x1E (Table 2-34) and an
auxiliary video stream descriptor (tag 0x2F, 2.6.74), which names its
coding with a stream type (aux_video_codedstreamtype) and carries its
supplemental information (si_rbsp() of ISO/IEC 23002-3).

Set the stream's codec from aux_video_codedstreamtype, probing it when
the descriptor is missing, and export the auxiliary video SI message as
AV_PKT_DATA_AUXILIARY_VIDEO_INFO, with an AV_PKT_DATA_AUXILIARY_ID of 2
for a depth map. The si_rbsp() reader goes in a file of its own, for the
program stream demuxer to share.

ISO/IEC 23002-3 is not freely available: si_rbsp() is read as TSDuck
reads it, and with an rbsp_trailing_bits() after the messages too, since
an RBSP ends with one.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
